      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Williamson%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A cobblestone Reformed Church, built between 1852 and 1863, once served the Dutch settlers before being repurposed and later demolished in the 1930s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/east_williamson_new_york"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "East Williamson’s early settlers were 156 Dutch immigrants from Zealand, Holland, who arrived in 1845 and built homes from lake‑washed cobblestones.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/east_williamson_new_york"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lake Ontario’s mild influence keeps East Williamson’s winters relatively moderate, with an average snowfall of 77 inches per year.",
